      "reasoning": "Article 8(2)(a)(iv) defines a war crime as extensive destruction of property not justified by military necessity and carried out wantonly. Although the bridge was used sporadically by the ABiH, the Trial Chamber found that its demolition was intended chiefly to sap Muslim morale, not to achieve a decisive military advantage. No evidence shows that the bridge’s loss was imperatively demanded for the conduct of hostilities; alternative routes or tactics were available. Consequently, the destruction fails the military‑necessity test and meets the statutory description of an unlawful, wanton act.",
